course: dictionary
lesson: 14544
title: A formal word for reading: perusal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Perusal is a formal noun. It names an action: the act of reading something. «The letter was sent to me for my perusal.» Letters and documents are often written in formal words like this one, so the context tells you the sentence is about reading.
explain: Look for the clue words. «After a careful perusal of the menu, Sam chose soup.» The word careful tells you that perusal means reading closely and thoroughly, not glancing. To check, swap in «reading carefully» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some people now use perusal more loosely, to mean a quick look. The dictionary notes this, so you may meet it. «Mia gave the newspaper a quick perusal before school.» The careful meaning is the older, proper one, and a quick look is the casual one.
fact: Perusal is a noun, so it names an action: the act of reading something.
fact: «Perusal» means reading something carefully and thoroughly.
fact: «For your perusal» means «for you to read».
fact: In modern use, perusal can also mean a quick look through something.
fact: Formal words like perusal often appear in letters, documents and notices.
exercise: «The letter was sent to me for my perusal.» What does perusal mean here? | *Reading it | Throwing it away | Sending it back to the post office | Drawing a picture of it
exercise: «After a careful perusal of the menu, Sam chose soup.» What does careful perusal mean? | *Reading closely and thoroughly | Singing the menu aloud | Losing the menu | A quick and careless glance
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to perusal, in its careful sense? | Shouting | Spilling | Ignoring | *Study
test: «The report is ready for your perusal, so please read it before Monday.» What is the report ready for? | *Your reading | Your lunch | Your pet | Your sleep
test: Mia gives the newspaper a quick perusal before school. What does perusal mean here? | Tearing it up | Copying it out by hand | Reading it aloud to a class | *A quick look through it
exam: What does perusal mean in «She made a careful perusal of the contract»? | Losing it | *Reading it closely and thoroughly | Ignoring it | Signing it quickly
